                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/497: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-29T22:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 29, 1919,
                                10 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10.46
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3387. American Mission’s 2863, June 28th, 10 p.m., and 2044 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">2924</hi>], July 2. Senator Eliodoro Yanez of Chile now
                    states that recent change of Government in Peru causes him to postpone the visit
                    he intended making to Washington for the purpose of discussing Tacna-Arica
                    matter. He expects to stay in France through August and will then probably
                    return to Chile.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">American Mission</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
